    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S643A\n\nSPONSOR: SEPULVEDA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the correction law, in relation to integrating community\nsupervision programs into an individual's employment, educational or\nvocational training schedule\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo permit parolees who are gainfully employed to attend required\nprograms outside of their work hours.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Correction Law § 201 (5) Section 2 provides an effec-\ntive date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPersons released from prison to community supervision are often required\nto take substance abuse treatment and other rehabilitative programs.\nPeople on community supervision also usually hold down jobs or enroll in\nschool or training programs. Parolees who maintain employment are far\nless likely to recidivate than parolees who do not work. When a parolee\nis able to secure gainful employment, it is important to ensure that he\nor she is able to work while completing necessary programs.\n\nThis bill would require DOCCS to allow an employed parolee to take such\nprograms during nonworking hours, such as nights and weekends, rather\nthan continuing the current practice of requiring them to miss days at\nwork and risk being fired in order to participate in programs during the\nbusiness day. Many programs offer their services on days, nights and\nweekends, or would do so in order to respond to the needs of their\nclients. Requiring parolees to quit or lose their jobs in order to\nattend programming violates one of the fundamental purposes of parole\nsupervision which is to help parolees secure employment and become\nproductive members of society. This bill provides DOCCS with flexibility\nbut makes it clear that it must make accommodations to ensure both\nprograms and employment are prioritized.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2020 - 2021 A.6977/S.643 (Davila/Sepulveda)\n\n2019 - 2020 A. 5104/S.1698 (Davila/Sepulveda)\n\n2018 - A.7605/5.8741 (Davila/Sepulveda)\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
